IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`
IMPORT `dg2-interested-definitions`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: section 144(a) to (d) -- INTERESTED DIRECTORS AND OFFICERS; CONTROLLING
-- STOCKHOLDER TRANSACTIONS; QUORUM; PRESUMPTIONS; LIABILITY OF A CONTROLLING STOCKHOLDER.
--
-- Three safe harbours (subsections (a), (b), (c)). Each says an act or transaction "may not be the subject of equitable relief, or
-- give rise to an award of damages" against the people named, if it was approved in one of the ways listed or is fair. The rules
-- here answer: is the act or transaction protected in that way? They do not decide the fairness (an input), whether a director is
-- disinterested (section 144(e), module dg2-interested-definitions) or any claim the safe harbour does not touch (subsection (d)(6)).
-- Judgments the text gives to the board ("the board has determined to be a disinterested director") or to a court (fairness) are inputs.
-- SEAT: a director or officer who is interested in a transaction; a minority stockholder who wants relief against it; a controlling
-- stockholder. The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Section 114(c)(2) takes paragraph (a)(2) out of the stockholder-to-member reading of section 114(a) for a nonprofit nonstock corporation.
-- Cross-reference taken as an input: section 251(h) (piece dg6).

§ `Section 144(d)(7): shares counted as voted`

DECLARE `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` HAS
-- out of range: section 251(h) (piece dg6): whether the act or transaction is an offer contemplated there is a plain input.
    `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vote was informed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vote was uncoerced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS A NUMBER
    `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `s 144(d)(7) Votes counted` HAS
    `the votes counted as cast` IS A NUMBER
    `the votes counted as cast in favor` IS A NUMBER

-- "Shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to an offer contemplated by section 251(h) of this title shall be
-- deemed voted in favor of the act or transaction and shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders that have not been
-- irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to such an offer shall be deemed voted against the act or transaction for
-- purposes of determining whether the act or transaction has been approved for purposes of paragraphs (a)(2), (b)(2), and (c)(1)."
-- For such an offer the votes counted are those deemed cast; otherwise the votes actually cast.
-- src:418 | (7) Shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to an offer contemplated by § 251(h) of this title shall be deemed voted in favor of the act or transaction and shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders that have not been irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to such an offer shall be deemed voted against the act or transaction for purposes of determining whether the act or transaction has been approved for purposes of paragraphs (a)(2), (b)(2), and (c)(1) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(7) (src:418)
GIVEN v IS A `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders`
GIVETH A `s 144(d)(7) Votes counted`
`s 144(d)(7) the votes counted` v MEANS
    IF   v's `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)`
    THEN `s 144(d)(7) Votes counted` WITH
             `the votes counted as cast` IS v's `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer`
                                            PLUS v's `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer`
           , `the votes counted as cast in favor` IS v's `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer`
    ELSE `s 144(d)(7) Votes counted` WITH
             `the votes counted as cast` IS v's `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders`
           , `the votes counted as cast in favor` IS v's `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders`

-- "an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders" (paragraphs (a)(2),
-- (b)(2)): the vote was informed, it was uncoerced, and more than half of the votes counted as cast were in favor.
-- src:397 | The act or transaction is approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(a)(2) (src:397)
GIVEN v IS A `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(a)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast` v MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (JUST (v's `the vote was informed` AND v's `the vote was uncoerced`))
        (`the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the votes cast`)
            ((`s 144(d)(7) the votes counted` v)'s `the votes counted as cast in favor`)
            ((`s 144(d)(7) the votes counted` v)'s `the votes counted as cast`))

§ `Section 144(a): interested directors and officers`

GIVETH A `Vote base`
`s 144(a)(1) the disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or such committee as a vote base` MEANS
    `another base named in the provision` "the disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or such committee"

GIVETH A `Vote base`
`s 144(a)(1) the directors of the corporation as a vote base` MEANS
    `another base named in the provision` "the directors of the corporation"

DECLARE `s 144(a) Facts` HAS
    `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and 1 or more of the corporation's directors or officers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and another entity in which 1 or more of its directors or officers are directors, stockholders, partners, managers, members, or officers, or have a financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction under subsection (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the material facts as to the director's or officer's relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction are disclosed or are known to all members of the board of directors or committee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction without gross negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or committee that authorized the act or transaction` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those disinterested directors who voted in favor` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of directors then serving on the board of directors` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those directors who are disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction` IS A NUMBER
    `a committee of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the act or transaction, approved or recommended it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS A `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders`
    `the act or transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a)(1): "The material facts ... are disclosed or are known to all members of the board of directors or a committee of the board of
-- directors, and the board or committee in good faith and without gross negligence authorizes the act or transaction by the
-- affirmative votes of a majority of the disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or such committee (as
-- applicable), even though the disinterested directors be less than a quorum; provided that if a majority of the directors are not
-- disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction, such act or transaction shall be approved (or recommended for
-- approval) by a committee of the board of directors that consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board of directors has
-- determined to be a disinterested director". The proviso adds a condition when more than half of the directors are not disinterested.
-- src:396 | (1) The material facts as to the director’s or officer’s relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction, including any involvement in the initiation, negotiation, or approval of the act or transaction, are disclosed or are known to all members of the board of directors or a committee of the board of directors, and the board or committee in good faith and without gross negligence authorizes the act or transaction by the affirmative votes of a majority of the disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or such committee (as applicable), even though the disinterested directors be less than a quorum; provided that if a majority of the directors are not disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction, such act or transaction shall be approved (or recommended for approval) by a committee of the board of directors that consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board of directors has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the act or transaction; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(a)(1) (src:396)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(a) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(a)(1) the disinterested directors authorized the act or transaction` f MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (JUST (   f's `the material facts as to the director's or officer's relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction are disclosed or are known to all members of the board of directors or committee`
              AND f's `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction in good faith`
              AND f's `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction without gross negligence`))
        (`dg2 both findings hold`
            (`the vote carries` (`a majority of` `s 144(a)(1) the disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or such committee as a vote base`)
                (f's `the number of those disinterested directors who voted in favor`)
                (f's `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or committee that authorized the act or transaction`))
            (CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `s 144(a)(1) the directors of the corporation as a vote base`)
                          ((f's `the number of directors then serving on the board of directors`) MINUS (f's `the number of those directors who are disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction`))
                          (f's `the number of directors then serving on the board of directors`)
             WHEN JUST notMajorityDisinterested THEN
                 JUST ((NOT notMajorityDisinterested) OR f's `a committee of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the act or transaction, approved or recommended it`)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING))

-- (a): "Except for a controlling stockholder transaction under subsection (b) or (c) of this section, an act or transaction involving
-- or between a corporation, or 1 or more of the corporation's subsidiaries, on the 1 hand, and 1 or more of the corporation's
-- directors or officers, on the other hand, or involving or between a corporation or 1 or more of the corporation's subsidiaries, on
-- the 1 hand, and any other corporation, partnership, ... in which 1 or more of its directors or officers are directors, stockholders,
-- partners, managers, members, or officers, or have a financial interest, on the other hand, may not be the subject of equitable
-- relief, or give rise to an award of damages, against a director or officer of the corporation because of the foregoing
-- circumstances or ... if: (1) ... or (2) ... or (3) The act or transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's
-- stockholders." The three limbs are alternatives. NOTHING for a controlling stockholder transaction (subsections (b) and (c) govern it)
-- and for an act or transaction outside both descriptions (the text does not say).
-- src:395 | (a) Except for a controlling stockholder transaction under subsection (b) or (c) of this section, an act or transaction involving or between a corporation, or 1 or more of the corporation’s subsidiaries, on the 1 hand, and 1 or more of the corporation’s directors or officers, on the other hand, or involving or between a corporation or 1 or more of the corporation’s subsidiaries, on the 1 hand, and any other corporation, partnership (general or limited), limited liability company, statutory trust, association, or any other entity or organization in which 1 or more of its directors or officers are directors, stockholders, partners, managers, members, or officers, or have a financial interest, on the other hand, may not be the subject of equitable relief, or give rise to an award of damages, against a director or officer of the corporation because of the foregoing circumstances or the receipt of any benefit by any such director, officer, entity, or organization or because the director or officer is present at or participates in the meeting of the board or committee which authorizes the act or transaction or was involved in the initiation, negotiation, or approval of the act or transaction (including by virtue of a director’s vote being counted for such purpose), if:
-- src:396 | (1) The material facts as to the director’s or officer’s relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction, including any involvement in the initiation, negotiation, or approval of the act or transaction, are disclosed or are known to all members of the board of directors or a committee of the board of directors, and the board or committee in good faith and without gross negligence authorizes the act or transaction by the affirmative votes of a majority of the disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or such committee (as applicable), even though the disinterested directors be less than a quorum; provided that if a majority of the directors are not disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction, such act or transaction shall be approved (or recommended for approval) by a committee of the board of directors that consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board of directors has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the act or transaction; or
-- src:397 | (2) The act or transaction is approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders; or
-- src:398 | (3) The act or transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation’s stockholders.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(a) (src:395-398)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(a) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(a) the act or transaction may not be the subject of equitable relief or give rise to damages against a director or officer` f MEANS
    IF   f's `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction under subsection (b) or (c)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   NOT (   f's `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and 1 or more of the corporation's directors or officers`
                   OR f's `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and another entity in which 1 or more of its directors or officers are directors, stockholders, partners, managers, members, or officers, or have a financial interest`)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE `dg2 either finding holds`
                  (`s 144(a)(1) the disinterested directors authorized the act or transaction` f)
                  (`dg2 either finding holds`
                      (`s 144(a)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast` (f's `the votes of the disinterested stockholders`))
                      (JUST (f's `the act or transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders`)))

§ `Section 144(b) and (c): controlling stockholder transactions`

GIVETH A `Vote base`
`s 144(b)(1) the disinterested directors then serving on the committee as a vote base` MEANS
    `another base named in the provision` "the disinterested directors then serving on the committee"

DECLARE `s 144(b) Facts` HAS
    `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act or transaction is a going private transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the material facts as to the controlling stockholder transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, are disclosed or are known to all members of the committee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the board of directors expressly delegated to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the controlling stockholder transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the committee approved or recommended the transaction in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the committee approved or recommended the transaction without gross negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the committee` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those disinterested directors who approved or recommended the transaction` IS A NUMBER
    `the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction is conditioned, by its terms as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS A `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders`
    `the transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (b)(1): material facts disclosed or known to all members of a committee to which the board has expressly delegated the authority to
-- negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the transaction, and the transaction is approved (or recommended) in good faith
-- and without gross negligence by a majority of the disinterested directors then serving on the committee, which consists of 2 or more
-- directors each determined by the board to be disinterested.
-- src:400 | (1) The material facts as to such controlling stockholder transaction (including the controlling stockholder’s or control group’s interest therein) are disclosed or are known to all members of a committee of the board of directors to which the board of directors has expressly delegated the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject such controlling stockholder transaction, and such controlling stockholder transaction is approved (or recommended for approval) in good faith and without gross negligence by a majority of the disinterested directors then serving on the committee; provided that the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board of directors has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the controlling stockholder transaction; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(b)(1) (src:400)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(b) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(b)(1) the committee of disinterested directors approved the controlling stockholder transaction` f MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (JUST (   f's `the material facts as to the controlling stockholder transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, are disclosed or are known to all members of the committee`
              AND f's `the board of directors expressly delegated to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the controlling stockholder transaction`
              AND f's `the committee approved or recommended the transaction in good faith`
              AND f's `the committee approved or recommended the transaction without gross negligence`
              AND f's `the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction`))
        (`the vote carries` (`a majority of` `s 144(b)(1) the disinterested directors then serving on the committee as a vote base`)
            (f's `the number of those disinterested directors who approved or recommended the transaction`)
            (f's `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the committee`))

-- (b)(2): "Such controlling stockholder transaction is conditioned, by its terms, as in effect at the time it is submitted to
-- stockholders for their approval or ratification, on the approval of or ratification by disinterested stockholders, and such
-- controlling stockholder transaction is approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes
-- cast by the disinterested stockholders". Both parts are required.
-- src:401 | (2) Such controlling stockholder transaction is conditioned, by its terms, as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders for their approval or ratification, on the approval of or ratification by disinterested stockholders, and such controlling stockholder transaction is approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(b)(2) (src:401)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(b) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(b)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved the controlling stockholder transaction as it conditioned` f MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (JUST (f's `the transaction is conditioned, by its terms as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders`))
        (`s 144(a)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast` (f's `the votes of the disinterested stockholders`))

-- (b): a controlling stockholder transaction (other than any going private transaction) "may not be the subject of equitable relief, or
-- give rise to an award of damages, against a director or officer of the corporation or any controlling stockholder or member of a
-- control group, by reason of a claim based on a breach of fiduciary duty by a director, officer, controlling stockholder, or member
-- of a control group, if: (1) ...; or (2) ...; or (3) Such controlling stockholder transaction is fair". The three limbs are alternatives.
-- src:399 | (b) A controlling stockholder transaction (other than any going private transaction) may not be the subject of equitable relief, or give rise to an award of damages, against a director or officer of the corporation or any controlling stockholder or member of a control group, by reason of a claim based on a breach of fiduciary duty by a director, officer, controlling stockholder, or member of a control group, if:
-- src:400 | (1) The material facts as to such controlling stockholder transaction (including the controlling stockholder’s or control group’s interest therein) are disclosed or are known to all members of a committee of the board of directors to which the board of directors has expressly delegated the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject such controlling stockholder transaction, and such controlling stockholder transaction is approved (or recommended for approval) in good faith and without gross negligence by a majority of the disinterested directors then serving on the committee; provided that the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board of directors has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the controlling stockholder transaction; or
-- src:401 | (2) Such controlling stockholder transaction is conditioned, by its terms, as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders for their approval or ratification, on the approval of or ratification by disinterested stockholders, and such controlling stockholder transaction is approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders; or
-- src:402 | (3) Such controlling stockholder transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation’s stockholders.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(b) (src:399-402)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(b) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(b) the controlling stockholder transaction may not be the subject of equitable relief or give rise to damages on a fiduciary claim` f MEANS
    IF   NOT f's `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   f's `the act or transaction is a going private transaction`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE `dg2 either finding holds`
                  (`s 144(b)(1) the committee of disinterested directors approved the controlling stockholder transaction` f)
                  (`dg2 either finding holds`
                      (`s 144(b)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved the controlling stockholder transaction as it conditioned` f)
                      (JUST (f's `the transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders`)))

-- (c): a controlling stockholder transaction constituting a going private transaction is protected if "(1) Such controlling stockholder
-- transaction is approved (or recommended for approval) in accordance with paragraph (b)(1) of this section and approved in accordance
-- with paragraph (b)(2) of this section; or (2) ... fair". Under limb (1) BOTH paragraphs are required.
-- src:403 | (c) A controlling stockholder transaction constituting a going private transaction may not be the subject of equitable relief, or give rise to an award of damages, against a director or officer of the corporation or any controlling stockholder or member of a control group by reason of a claim based on breach of fiduciary duty by a director, officer, controlling stockholder, or member of a control group, if:
-- src:404 | (1) Such controlling stockholder transaction is approved (or recommended for approval) in accordance with paragraph (b)(1) of this section and approved in accordance with paragraph (b)(2) of this section; or
-- src:405 | (2) Such controlling stockholder transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation’s stockholders.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(c) (src:403-405)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(b) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(c) the going private transaction may not be the subject of equitable relief or give rise to damages on a fiduciary claim` f MEANS
    IF   NOT f's `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   NOT f's `the act or transaction is a going private transaction`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE `dg2 either finding holds`
                  (`dg2 both findings hold`
                      (`s 144(b)(1) the committee of disinterested directors approved the controlling stockholder transaction` f)
                      (`s 144(b)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved the controlling stockholder transaction as it conditioned` f))
                  (JUST (f's `the transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders`))

§ `Section 144(d): quorum, presumptions, and what the safe harbours leave open`

-- (d)(1): "Common or interested directors may be counted in determining the presence of a quorum at a meeting of the board of
-- directors or of a committee which authorizes the act or transaction." Only for such a meeting; for any other the text does not say.
-- src:406 | (d) (1) Common or interested directors may be counted in determining the presence of a quorum at a meeting of the board of directors or of a committee which authorizes the act or transaction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(1) (src:406)
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting of the board of directors or of a committee which authorizes the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(1) common or interested directors may be counted in determining the presence of a quorum` `the meeting is a meeting of the board of directors or of a committee which authorizes the act or transaction` MEANS
    IF   `the meeting is a meeting of the board of directors or of a committee which authorizes the act or transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (d)(2): "Any director of a corporation that has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange shall be presumed to be a
-- disinterested director with respect to an act or transaction to which such director is not a party if the board of directors shall
-- have determined that such director satisfies the applicable criteria for determining director independence from the corporation and,
-- if applicable with respect to the act or transaction, the controlling stockholder or control group, under the rules (and
-- interpretations thereof) promulgated by such exchange ..., which presumption shall be heightened and may only be rebutted by
-- substantial and particularized facts that such director has a material interest in such act or transaction or has a material
-- relationship with a person with a material interest in such act or transaction."
-- src:407 | (2) Any director of a corporation that has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange shall be presumed to be a disinterested director with respect to an act or transaction to which such director is not a party if the board of directors shall have determined that such director satisfies the applicable criteria for determining director independence from the corporation and, if applicable with respect to the act or transaction, the controlling stockholder or control group, under the rules (and interpretations thereof) promulgated by such exchange (treating the applicable controlling stockholder and control group as if the controlling stockholder and control group were the corporation for purposes of applying such criteria to determine independence from a controlling stockholder or control group), which presumption shall be heightened and may only be rebutted by substantial and particularized facts that such director has a material interest in such act or transaction or has a material relationship with a person with a material interest in such act or transaction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(2) (src:407)
GIVEN `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is a party to the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board of directors has determined that the director satisfies the applicable exchange criteria for independence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(2) the director is presumed to be a disinterested director` `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` `the director is a party to the act or transaction` `the board of directors has determined that the director satisfies the applicable exchange criteria for independence` MEANS
        `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange`
    AND (NOT `the director is a party to the act or transaction`)
    AND `the board of directors has determined that the director satisfies the applicable exchange criteria for independence`

-- src:407 | which presumption shall be heightened and may only be rebutted by substantial and particularized facts that such director has a material interest in such act or transaction or has a material relationship with a person with a material interest in such act or transaction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(2) (src:407)
GIVEN `substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material interest in the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material relationship with a person with a material interest in the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(2) the presumption is rebutted` `substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material interest in the act or transaction` `substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material relationship with a person with a material interest in the act or transaction` MEANS
        `substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material interest in the act or transaction`
    OR  `substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material relationship with a person with a material interest in the act or transaction`

-- (d)(3): "The designation, nomination, or vote in the election of the director to the board of directors by any person that has a
-- material interest in an act or transaction shall not, of itself, be evidence that a director is not a disinterested director".
-- src:408 | (3) The designation, nomination, or vote in the election of the director to the board of directors by any person that has a material interest in an act or transaction shall not, of itself, be evidence that a director is not a disinterested director with respect to an act or transaction to which such director is not a party.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(3) (src:408)
GIVEN `a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction designated or nominated the director or voted in the election of the director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(3) the designation, nomination or vote is of itself evidence that the director is not a disinterested director` `a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction designated or nominated the director or voted in the election of the director` MEANS
    FALSE

-- (d)(4): "No person shall be deemed a controlling stockholder unless such person satisfies the criteria in paragraph (e)(2) of this
-- section. No 2 or more persons that are not controlling stockholders shall be a control group unless they satisfy the criteria in
-- paragraph (e)(1) of this section." The rules of section 144(e) are the criteria.
-- src:409 | No person shall be deemed a controlling stockholder unless such person satisfies the criteria in paragraph (e)(2) of this section. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(4) (src:409)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(e)(2) Facts about a person's control`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(4) the person may be deemed a controlling stockholder` f MEANS
    `s 144(e)(2) the person is a controlling stockholder` f

-- src:409 | No 2 or more persons that are not controlling stockholders shall be a control group unless they satisfy the criteria in paragraph (e)(1) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(4) (src:409)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(e)(1) Facts about a group of persons`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(4) the persons may be a control group` f MEANS
    `s 144(e)(1) the persons are a control group` f

-- (d)(5): "No person who is a controlling stockholder or member of a control group shall be liable in such capacity to the
-- corporation or its stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty other than for: a. A breach of the duty of
-- loyalty to the corporation or the other stockholders; b. Acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional
-- misconduct or a knowing violation of law; or c. Any transaction from which the person derived an improper personal benefit."
-- The answer says whether this subsection shields the person from monetary damages for the kind of breach. NOTHING if the person is
-- neither a controlling stockholder nor a member of a control group.
DECLARE `s 144(d)(5) Kind of breach` IS ONE OF
    `a breach of the duty of loyalty to the corporation or the other stockholders`
    `acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law`
    `a transaction from which the person derived an improper personal benefit`
    `a breach of fiduciary duty of any other kind`

-- src:410 | (5) No person who is a controlling stockholder or member of a control group shall be liable in such capacity to the corporation or its stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty other than for:
-- src:411 | a. A breach of the duty of loyalty to the corporation or the other stockholders;
-- src:412 | b. Acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law; or
-- src:413 | c. Any transaction from which the person derived an improper personal benefit.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(5) (src:410-413)
GIVEN `the person is a controlling stockholder or a member of a control group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of breach` IS A `s 144(d)(5) Kind of breach`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(5) the person is shielded from monetary damages for the breach` `the person is a controlling stockholder or a member of a control group` `the kind of breach` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the person is a controlling stockholder or a member of a control group`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of breach`
         WHEN `a breach of the duty of loyalty to the corporation or the other stockholders` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a transaction from which the person derived an improper personal benefit` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a breach of fiduciary duty of any other kind` THEN JUST TRUE

-- (d)(6): "Nothing in subsection (a), (b), or (c) of this section shall: a. Limit or eliminate the right of any person to seek
-- equitable relief on the grounds that an act or transaction, including a controlling stockholder transaction, was not authorized or
-- approved in compliance with the procedures set forth in this chapter, was not authorized or approved in compliance with the
-- certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, or is in violation of any plan, agreement, or order of any governmental
-- authority to which the corporation is a party or subject; or b. Limit judicial review for purposes of injunctive relief of provisions
-- or devices designed or intended to deter, delay, or preclude a change of control or other transaction involving the corporation or a
-- change in the composition of the board of directors; or c. Limit or eliminate the right of any person to seek relief on the grounds
-- that a stockholder or other person knowingly aided and abetted a breach of fiduciary duty by 1 or more of the directors".
DECLARE `s 144(d)(6) Ground of a claim` IS ONE OF
    `that the act or transaction was not authorized or approved in compliance with the procedures set forth in this chapter`
    `that the act or transaction was not authorized or approved in compliance with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws`
    `that the act or transaction is in violation of a plan, agreement, or order of a governmental authority to which the corporation is a party or subject`
    `that a provision or device is designed or intended to deter, delay, or preclude a change of control or other transaction or a change in the composition of the board, and injunctive relief is sought`
    `that a stockholder or other person knowingly aided and abetted a breach of fiduciary duty by 1 or more of the directors`
    `a ground of any other kind`

-- src:414 | (6) Nothing in subsection (a), (b), or (c) of this section shall:
-- src:415 | a. Limit or eliminate the right of any person to seek equitable relief on the grounds that an act or transaction, including a controlling stockholder transaction, was not authorized or approved in compliance with the procedures set forth in this chapter, was not authorized or approved in compliance with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, or is in violation of any plan, agreement, or order of any governmental authority to which the corporation is a party or subject; or
-- src:416 | b. Limit judicial review for purposes of injunctive relief of provisions or devices designed or intended to deter, delay, or preclude a change of control or other transaction involving the corporation or a change in the composition of the board of directors; or
-- src:417 | c. Limit or eliminate the right of any person to seek relief on the grounds that a stockholder or other person knowingly aided and abetted a breach of fiduciary duty by 1 or more of the directors of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(d)(6) (src:414-417)
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `s 144(d)(6) Ground of a claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(d)(6) subsections (a), (b) and (c) leave the right to seek relief on the ground open` `the ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `a ground of any other kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
